HOW TO DELETE TRADES AND SESSIONS IN THE JOURNAL
How to Delete Trades and Sessions in the Journal

Backtesting Journal

Can I delete individual trades?
Individual trades in the Backtesting Journal cannot be deleted on their own. Trades are tied to the session they were placed in — to remove trades, you need to delete the entire session.

How to delete a session
1. Go to Testing → Sessions
2. Select the session you want to delete from the dropdown at the top
3. Click the red Delete session button in the top right
4. Confirm the deletion

This is permanent. Deleting a session removes all trades, stats, and analytics associated with it. This cannot be undone.

I just want to make changes to my session, not delete it
Use Session Settings instead — you can edit the session name, strategy, starting balance, assets, spreads, commissions, and date range without losing any data.

Live Journal

How to delete a trade
1. Open the trade you want to delete (trade detail view)
2. Select Delete
3. Confirm

Deleted trades cannot be recovered from within the journal. If your broker account is still connected, triggering a re-sync may restore the trade. If not, contact support.

Frequently Asked Questions

Can I delete individual trades in the Backtesting Journal?
No — trades are tied to their session. Delete the entire session from Testing → Sessions to remove them.

Can I recover a deleted session?
No — session deletion is permanent and cannot be undone.

I accidentally deleted a Live Journal trade. Can I get it back?
Deleted trades cannot be recovered from within the journal. If your broker is still connected, a re-sync may restore it. Otherwise contact support.

