TRADING ON SECONDS TIMEFRAMES IN FOREX AND FUTURES MARKETS
Trading on Seconds Timeframes in Forex and Futures Markets
Trading on Seconds Timeframes in Forex and Futures Markets

Seconds-based timeframes allow traders to analyze price action with greater precision, making them especially useful for scalping, execution refinement, and detailed replay analysis.

Availability

Seconds timeframes are only available on the Pro plan.

If you're currently on the Intermediate plan or a lower plan, you won’t be able to access seconds charts. To use this feature, you’ll need to upgrade to the Pro plan.

Supported Assets and Minimum Timeframes

Seconds timeframes vary depending on the asset type:

Futures Markets
Supports timeframes as low as 1 second
Examples: 1s, 5s, 10s, and higher

This allows for more detailed analysis and is especially useful for traders who want to review fast market movements with maximum precision.

Forex (CFD Pairs)
Supports timeframes as low as 5 seconds
Examples: 5s, 10s, 15s, and higher
1-second timeframes are not available for CFD pairs

In other words, if you're trading futures assets, you can use the 1-second chart. If you're trading CFD pairs, the lowest available seconds timeframe is 5 seconds.

How to Use Seconds Timeframes
Open a chart in FX Replay
Click the timeframe selector
Select a seconds-based timeframe such as 5s or 10s
Start your replay or analysis session

Note: If you don’t see seconds timeframes, make sure you are on the Pro plan and that your selected asset supports the timeframe you want to use.

Why Use Seconds Timeframes?
Fine-tune trade entries and exits
Analyze micro price movements
Improve execution during replay sessions
Practice fast-paced trading and scalping strategies
Common Questions
Why can’t I access seconds charts?

Seconds charts are available only on the Pro plan. If you're on the Intermediate plan or lower, this feature will not appear in your chart options.

Why can I use 1-second charts on futures but not on forex pairs?

The 1-second timeframe is supported only for futures assets. For CFD pairs, the lowest available seconds timeframe is 5 seconds.

